---
import Retro from "../layouts/Retro.astro";

const releaseLatest = "https://github.com/leomosley/vole/releases/latest";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Is this actually a trojan?",
    a: "No. It's a genuine open-source Windows tray app. The site is a joke about looking like one \u2014 read the source before trusting us.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why does Windows say \u201Cunknown publisher\u201D?",
    a: "The installer is unsigned, so SmartScreen warns. Click <i>More info \u2192 Run anyway</i>.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will it get me banned?",
    a: "It uses the standard RegisterHotKey mechanism, not low-level hooks, to stay compatible with Vanguard, EAC and BattlEye.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does it phone home?",
    a: "No cloud, no account, no telemetry. Config is a JSON file in %APPDATA%\\VOLE.",
  },
];
---

<Retro
  title="VOLE.EXE :: DOCS & F.A.Q."
  tagline="* R.T.F.M. * READ THE FRIENDLY MANUAL *"
  active="docs"
>
  <section class="panel">
    <h2>HOW IT WORKS</h2>
    <p>
      VOLE is a single native <b>Rust</b> binary in your system tray. It listens for
      your global hotkeys; on a keypress it reaches into the Windows volume mixer
      (Core Audio) and changes the volume of the apps you chose. The config window
      is only built when you open it, so gaming costs nothing.
    </p>
    <p>The whole model is three words:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Hotkey</b> &mdash; a key combo (e.g. <code>Ctrl+Alt+G</code>) with
        one or more actions, optionally a <b>toggle</b>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Target</b> &mdash; a named process (<code>Discord.exe</code>) or the
        <code>foreground</code> window.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Operation</b> &mdash; <code>set</code> a level, <code>adjust</code> by
        a delta, or <code>mute</code>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Mark a hotkey <b>toggle</b> and the first press snapshots current volumes; the
      next restores them. That's how "set to 20%" becomes a duck.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel install">
    <h2>INSTALLING</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Grab the latest <code>VOLE-Setup-*.exe</code> from
        <a href={releaseLatest} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >GitHub Releases</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        Run it (it elevates to admin) and, on the SmartScreen warning, choose
        <i>More info &rarr; Run anyway</i>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open the tray icon &rarr; <i>Open config</i>, bind your hotkeys, and use
        the per-app <i>Test-fire</i> button to confirm the right session.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="install__admin">
      <img src="/vole.png" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
      <p>
        <b>Why admin?</b> Windows won't deliver hotkeys to a lower-privilege app while
        an elevated, anti-cheat-protected game is focused. Running elevated keeps
        your hotkeys alive mid-match.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a
      class="install__cta"
      href={releaseLatest}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
      data-blip
    >
      &#9660; DOWNLOAD THE INSTALLER &#9660;
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="panel faq">
    <h2>F.A.Q.</h2>
    <dl>
      {
        faqs.map((f) => (
          <>
            <dt>{f.q}</dt>
            <dd set:html={f.a} />
          </>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
    <p class="faq__foot">
      More in <a
        href="https://github.com/leomosley/vole"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">the repository</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    code {
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid var(--silver-dark);
      padding: 0 4px;
      font-family: "Courier New", monospace;
    }

    .install ol {
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .install__admin {
      display: flex;
      gap: 12px;
      align-items: flex-start;
      background: #fff8dc;
      border: 2px dashed #b8860b;
      padding: 10px 12px;
      margin: 12px 0;
    }
    .install__admin img {
      image-rendering: pixelated;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }
    .install__admin p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    .install__cta {
      display: inline-block;
      text-align: center;
      font-family: "Impact", sans-serif;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      font-size: 22px;
      color: #fff;
      text-decoration: none;
      padding: 12px 20px;
      background: linear-gradient(#3a7bff, #0033aa);
      border: 4px outset #9dc0ff;
      box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    }

    .faq dt {
      font-weight: bold;
      color: #7a0000;
      font-family: "Arial", sans-serif;
      margin-top: 12px;
    }
    .faq dd {
      margin: 4px 0 0;
      padding-left: 16px;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--silver);
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .faq__foot {
      font-style: italic;
      margin-top: 16px;
    }
  </style>
</Retro>
